### Ron's Coffee. Ron runs a stalkerware / identity-tracking operation.

=== ron
-- start
? flag.ron_resolved -> after
? flag.knows_ron_secret -> confront
RON: Welcome to Ron's. Best coffee in the neighborhood, which isn't saying much around here. What'll it be?
* "Just coffee." -> coffee
* [SPEECH 20] "You run the whole operation off the shop wifi? Brave." -> fish | coffee
* "Nothing. Just looking." -> looking
-- coffee
RON: One coffee. On the house for a regular. You are a regular now. I decide that.
! give coffee 1
-> END
-- fish
RON: ...I don't know what you mean. It's a coffee shop. Beans, milk, a card reader. That's the whole business.
ELLIOT (V.O.): He blinked twice on 'the whole business.' There's a back room. There's always a back room.
! set found_ron_code ; set ron_backroom_hint
-> END
-- looking
RON: Look all you want. Buy something eventually.
-> END
-- confront
ELLIOT (V.O.): I know what he sells now. Not coffee. Access. The ability to follow people who spent everything to get away. He sells the leash back to the people they ran from.
RON: You've been in my server. I can see it on your face, the way you're looking at me like I'm a thing under glass.
* "Your customers are stalkers. Every one of them. You made that market." -> accuse
* [HACKING 40] "I own your server now. Say one wrong word and it all goes to the FBI." -> own | accuse
* "I don't care what you do. I need the server. That's all." -> transactional
-- accuse
RON: I sell software. What people do with it — that's on them. I never touched anyone.
ELLIOT (V.O.): The oldest lie. The one that lets everyone with clean hands sleep. Build the weapon, sell the weapon, and it's never your finger on the trigger.
-> decide
-- own
RON: ...Okay. Okay. What do you want. Money? I've got money. Just don't send it anywhere.
ELLIOT (V.O.): Fear. Finally. The only language his kind ever really learns.
! set ron_afraid
-> decide
-- transactional
RON: A businessman. I can work with a businessman. The server's yours to poke at. Just leave my customer list out of it.
-> decide
-- decide
ELLIOT (V.O.): I could report him. Slow, official, maybe nothing. I could expose him — dump the list, let his customers find out they're on it. I could take the list myself. Or I could just take what fsociety wants and walk.
* [require q.sq_ron>=20] Report him to the FBI. Let the system be slow and sure. -> report
* [require q.sq_ron>=20] Expose the whole operation. Publish everything. -> expose
* [require q.sq_ron>=20] Take the customer list. Keep the leverage. -> take
* "Just give me the server. I'm not the police." -> walk
-- report
ELLIOT (V.O.): I send the file to a tip line that actually reads them. Rare. It'll take months. But it's clean, and Ron's name is on a desk somewhere now, waiting.
! quest sq_ron done ; fame nypd 4 ; fame locals 3 ; set ron_reported ; stab 4 ; set ron_resolved
RON: You reported me. God. You people. You think a form fixes anything.
-> plant_offer
-- expose
ELLIOT (V.O.): I push the whole thing live. Every customer, every victim, every card number. It's not justice. It's a bomb in a crowded room. Some of the people it frees, it also burns. I press the key anyway.
! quest sq_ron done ; fame fsociety 5 ; infamy nypd 3 ; set ron_exposed ; stab -3 ; set ron_resolved
RON: You have no idea what you just did. Those lists — some of those people were hiding for good reasons too.
-> plant_offer
-- take
ELLIOT (V.O.): I copy the list to a drive and slip it in my pocket. Thousands of names. Power, distilled. I tell myself I'll use it well. Everyone tells themselves that.
! give stalker_db 1 ; quest sq_ron done ; set ron_walked_away ; stab -2 ; infamy locals 1 ; set ron_resolved
-> plant_offer
-- walk
ELLIOT (V.O.): Not my circus. Not tonight. I take what I came for and leave Ron to whatever finds him first.
! quest sq_ron 50 ; set ron_walked_away ; set ron_resolved
-> plant_offer
-- after
? !flag.rootkit_planted -> plant_offer
? flag.ron_reported -> after_reported
? flag.ron_exposed -> after_exposed
RON: You. Coffee's four dollars. For you it's five. Get out of my line.
-> END
-- after_reported
RON: A lawyer came by. Then two men in suits who didn't drink anything. Are you happy? Don't answer. Just leave.
-> END
-- after_exposed
> Ron is wiping a counter that is already clean. He doesn't look up.
RON: Half my regulars won't come in anymore. The other half come in to look at me. Go away, Elliot.
-> END
-- plant_offer
ELLIOT (V.O.): Either way, the server's open now. And fsociety wants a rootkit in it — a doorway into E Corp's honeypot, one hop away.
* Plant the rootkit. -> plant
* Not yet. -> END
-- plant
? flag.rootkit_planted -> END
ELLIOT (V.O.): The rootkit slides home. Ron's little server is a fsociety asset now. And through it, a thread runs all the way up to the top of the tower.
! set rootkit_planted ; quest mq_rootkit 40 ; quest mq_rootkit 50 ; quest mq_rootkit done ; xp 40
ELLIOT (V.O.): My phone buzzes. Unknown number. One line: 'Nice work. Come to the Delancey Street station. Alone. — a friend.' The city just got smaller.
! quest mq_fsociety 10
-> END
